-- title:
--   Conjugation by diag(varpiᵥ,1)z(u) preserves Z(K)N(A)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $v$ be a nonzero prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$ (a point of the height-one spectrum), let $u$ be a unit of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_K$ of $K$, and let $y$ be an element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ (the group `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 K) K`). Write $H =$ `rationalCentreUnipotent K` for the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ generated by the union of the image of $K^\times$ under $a \mapsto \mathrm{diag}(a,a)$ (scalar matrices over $K$, pushed into the adeles by `globalPoints`) and the image of the additive group $\mathbb{A}_K$ under $x \mapsto \begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, that is the join $Z(K) \vee N(\mathbb{A}_K)$ of these two ranges. Let $b =$ `heckeGen (𝓞 K) K v * centralScalar (𝓞 K) K u`, the product of $\mathrm{diag}(\tau,1)$, where $\tau$ is the idele which is the chosen uniformiser of $v$ at $v$ and a unit elsewhere (the image of `uniformizerUnit K v` under `localUnit` followed by the inclusion of the finite into the full adeles), with the central scalar $\mathrm{diag}(u,u)$. The assertion is the equivalence $y \in H \iff b\,y\,b^{-1} \in H$.
--
--   The element $b$ thus normalises $Z(K)N(\mathbb{A}_K)$, which is what makes the shift $Hg \mapsto Hbg$ well defined on the quotient $Z(K)N(\mathbb{A}_K)\backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$. It is used in the Rankin–Selberg part of the development, in [`AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.exists_hasProd_quotientIntegral_eq_sPartIntegral_mul_of_shell_recursion`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.exists_hasProd_quotientIntegral_eq_sPartIntegral_mul_of_shell_recursion), where integrals over the quotient are compared after shifting by one Iwasawa shell at $v$.
